MangoHud: add exec2= that renders like a built-in field
=======================================================

Problem
-------
`exec=$HOME/scripts/pad-battery.py` prints "PAD 45%", but the line lands in
the HUD at roughly half the height of the CPU/GPU rows and is entirely white,
so it reads as a footnote rather than as a peer of the other stats.

Root cause
----------
Two separate things, both in `_exec()` (src/hud_elements.cpp):

1. Size. `_exec()` opens with `ImGui::PushFont(sw_stats->font_secondary)`.
   `font_size_secondary` defaults to `font_size * 0.55` when unset
   (src/overlay_params.cpp, "If secondary font size not set, compute it from
   main font_size"), so with `font_size=20` the exec line renders at 11px.
   `cpu_stats()`/`gpu_stats()` never push a font at all — they draw into the
   ambient `Fonts[0]` at the full `font_size`, and only push `font_small` for
   the unit suffix ("%", "MHz", "W"). So `exec` sits in the same size class as
   gamemode / resolution / engine_version, not the CPU/GPU rows.

2. Colour. `_exec()` emits the whole string through a single
   `TextColored(colors.text, ...)`. `HudElements::TextColored` is just
   vsnprintf + RenderOutlinedText, with no markup parsing anywhere, and there
   is no per-element colour option for exec. Built-in fields get their look
   from doing two draws — label in `colors.engine`, value in `colors.text`
   (see `gamemode()` and `device_battery()`).

Why not just set font_size_secondary
------------------------------------
`font_size_secondary=20` fixes the height, but `font_secondary` is shared by
gamemode, vkbasalt, resolution, show_fps_limit, engine_version, vulkan_driver
and winesync, so all of them grow too, and long strings can overlap the label
column because the column width math does not account for it
(MangoHud issue #1913). It also cannot give the label a colour.

Fix
---
Add a separate `exec2=` parameter next to `exec=`, leaving `exec=` untouched.
`_exec2()` drops the `PushFont` so the output uses the primary font, then
splits the command output on the first space and draws the first token with
`colors.engine` and the remainder with `colors.text`, matching the two-draw
shape of `gamemode()` and `device_battery()`. With the stock palette
(engine_color=eb5b5b, text_color=ffffff) "PAD 45%" comes out as a red PAD and
a white 45% at the same height as the CPU and GPU rows.

Alignment. The built-ins pass their value through `right_aligned_text()`,
which sets the cursor to `pos.x + off_x - CalcTextSize(value).x`
(src/overlay.cpp). `off_x` is `ralign_width`, only four characters wide
(`CalcTextSize("A").x * 4`, src/overlay.cpp), so any value longer than that
produces a negative offset and is drawn back on top of the label — "PAD 80%"
is fine but "PAD missing" and "PAD 45% chg" collide. The HUD table is created
with `ImGuiTableFlags_NoClip`, so nothing truncates it. `_exec2()` therefore
right-aligns only while the value fits in `ralign_width` and otherwise draws
it in place, claiming the column it spills into.

Output with no space in it falls back to a single `colors.engine` draw.
`exec2` entries share `exec_list`, so `update_exec()` runs their commands on
the same schedule as `exec` with no extra plumbing.

Upstream: not submitted. Related reports about the same limitation are
MangoHud issues #1013, #1808 and #1913.

